<title>CANADA: Ontario says to present 1997/98 budget on May 6.</title>
<headline>Ontario says to present 1997/98 budget on May 6.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Ontario, Canada's most populous province, said on Monday that it would present its 1997/98 budget on Tuesday, May 6.</p>
<p>The provincial budget for the fiscal year ended March 31 will be delivered at 1600 EDT/2000 GMT, Finance Minister Ernie Eves said in a statement.</p>
<p>In February, Eves revised the government's 1996/97 budget deficit to C$7.67 billion, down C$508 million from his original budget forecast.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
